{
"v": 1,
"name": "alexandra konstantinovna",
"bio": [
"I build environments, and the creatures and objects that live inside them. Trained in Fine Art at Central Saint Martins, I spent years as a set designer for fashion, film and editorial, so I still treat every work as a set: a place with its own logic, materials and rules, that someone can step into.",
"I move between VR and mixed reality, 3D modelling, machine learning, microcontrollers, ceramics, glass, paint and melted plastic. I call this imaginary engineering: working prototypes for systems that don't exist yet, built with whatever is at hand.",
"Currently: applying high-tech solutions to sparking useless conversations."
],
"works": [
{
"id": "01",
"title": "imaginary engineering / guardian",
"years": "2026",
"prov": "human",
"tags": [
"sculpture",
"electronics",
"VR / MR",
"drawing"
],
"desc": "Submarine installation and its guardian, an insect prototype in steel and torch-fused glass beads with an ESP32 brain, ultrasonic sensor and TFT eyes. Glass eyes replicate the mechanics of both the human eye and the oculus lens, and react to the distance of the viewer. The guardian is part of the submarine: a living quarters that travels between 2025 and 2005.",
"spec": [
[
"physical",
"a living prototype 002"
],
[
"digital",
"in production of V3"
],
[
"function",
"identification and protection"
],
[
"materials",
"steel, glass, ESP32, web dashboard"
]
],
